    "updated_at": "2017-05-03T10:54:18Z",
    "body": "When I add a `download` attribute Chrome downloads and Firefox shows a download dialog. Safari doesn't do anything different. So it seems like you would branch first on the download attribute and then if there's no such attribute maybe return (no exception) if the targeting hits the popup blocker.\r\n\r\nThat should further simplify the algorithms we have today.",
